{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/98713-let-s-discuss-brute-force","id":98713,"title":"Let's discuss: Brute Force","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T15:34:55-07:00","id":98713,"title":"Let's discuss: Brute Force","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I'm starting a cross-splat game soon and I'll be playing a Brute Force Promethean. I really like the mood and feel of brute force, but the first dot (will = 9-again) seems..........useless?<br /> <br /> You basically need 24 dice for it to outdamage a regular willpower of +3 dice. So I was thinking of ways to put it back on track and I thought: Why not a simple 4 dice for willpower (instead of 3) or something along the lines of &quot;Ignore [Brute Force] points of armor from your opponent when spending a willpower point&quot;?<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> Magnum Opus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:07:56-07:00","id":98738,"title":"","content":"The houserules I use for Brute Force:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houserules</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 to learn this style, Strength \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 (temporary or permanently) to use this style, Brawl \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Smash \u2022</b> (renamed from Falling Pillar)<br /> 9-again on all Brawl attacks, even without Willpower expenditure.<br /> <br /> <b>Juggernaut \u2022\u2022</b> (moved here from \u2022\u2022\u2022 for balance reasons)<br /> No rule changes.<br /> <br /> <b>Crush and bite \u2022\u2022\u2022</b> (moved here from \u2022\u2022 for balance reasons)<br /> No rule changes.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Cracker \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><br /> Removed loss of Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The prerequisites were changed to really make it require brute force. &quot;Juggernaut&quot; and &quot;Crush and Bite&quot; were exchanged as doing Lethal instead of Bashing usually is at higher levels than just increased damage. The last power just isn't strong enough to merit the loss of Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T02:57:25-07:00","id":99041,"title":"","content":"9-again is great for something like Brute Force as it rewards you for creating huge dicepools. It is not worth Willpower though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}